# Oracle 10.2.0.5's reply to a WRITE of 01 02 03 04 (4 bytes) into a temporary
# BLOB (#2803): the locator, the amount echoed (01 04), the status.
# Captured 2026-11-27 through tools/capture_proxy.py. The TTC payload,
# without the packet's header, as `hexdump -C` output; the offset column
# and the |ascii| gutter are ignored by tests.replay.parse_hexdump.
00000000  08 00 26 00 01 01 08 00  03 00 01 00 00 22 37 91  |..&.........."7.|
00000010  00 00 00 00 02 00 00 00  0a 00 00 00 01 00 00 00  |................|
00000020  00 1e f2 d8 bb c3 30 03  46 01 04 04 01 01 01 0b  |......0.F.......|
00000030  00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00  00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00  |................|
00000040  00 00 00 0e 00 01 01 00  00 00 00                 |...........|
0000004b
